<title>NETHERLANDS: Volker, Kondor -- key ratios.</title>
<headline>Volker, Kondor -- key ratios.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch construction firms Volker Stevin and Kondor Wessels Groep said on Tuesday they were in merger talks aimed at creating the Netherlands' second largest construction group after HBG .</p>
<p>Below are a few of the key ratios taken from Reuters Securities 3000:</p>
<p>				    Volker Stevin     Kondor Wessels</p>
<p>				   (calendar 1995) (yr to end-June 1996)</p>
<p>    Shr price (0930 GMT) (Dfl)   200.00		88.90</p>
<p>    Market Cap (Dfl million)     983.38	     483.61</p>
<p>    Workforce			   8,758		2,023</p>
<p>    Earnings per share		12.00		 5.23 (1995)</p>
<p>    Consensus est. for 1996 EPS   13.10		 6.60</p>
<p>    Revenue (Dfl billion)	    2.66		 1.07</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit (Dfl million)  57.89		53.98</p>
<p>    Ratios: PE			  15.70		16.58</p>
<p>    Operating margin (pct)	   2.16		 5.26</p>
<p>    Return on Equity (pct)	  15.09		19.28</p>
<p>    Book Value Per Share	    74.18		32.93</p>
<p>    Return on Total Assets (pct)   4.37		 5.69</p>
